\"chain init failed\".into()))?;\n",[278,658,660],{"class":280,"line":659},27,[278,661,297],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":296},[278,663,665],{"class":280,"line":664},28,[278,666,667],{},"\u002F\u002F 3. Render a chat prompt and run the constrained completion.\n",[278,669,671],{"class":280,"line":670},29,[278,672,673],{},"let messages = vec![\n",[278,675,677],{"class":280,"line":676},30,[278,678,679],{},"    ChatMessage::new(Role::System, \"Return only JSON.\"),\n",[278,681,683],{"class":280,"line":682},31,[278,684,685],{},"    ChatMessage::new(Role::User, \"Create one fictional person.\"),\n",[278,687,689],{"class":280,"line":688},32,[278,690,691],{},"];\n",[278,693,695],{"class":280,"line":694},33,[278,696,697],{},"let prompt = render_builtin(BuiltinTemplate::ChatMl, &messages, &[], true);\n",[278,699,701],{"class":280,"line":700},34,[278,702,297],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":296},[278,704,706],{"class":280,"line":705},35,[278,707,708],{},"let response = llama.create_completion_with_sampler(\n",[278,710,712],{"class":280,"line":711},36,[278,713,714],{},"    &prompt,\n",[278,716,718],{"class":280,"line":717},37,[278,719,720],{},"    CompletionOptions::new(96),\n",[278,722,724],{"class":280,"line":723},38,[278,725,726],{},"    &mut sampler,\n",[278,728,730],{"class":280,"line":729},39,[278,731,732],{},")?;\n",[278,734,736],{"class":280,"line":735},40,[278,737,297],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":296},[278,739,741],{"class":280,"line":740},41,[278,742,743],{},"\u002F\u002F 4. Parse the result.\n",[278,745,747],{"class":280,"line":746},42,[278,748,749],{},"let parsed: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_str(&response.text)?;\n",[278,751,753],{"class":280,"line":752},43,[278,754,755],{},"println!(\"{}\", serde_json::to_string_pretty(&parsed)?);\n",[223,757,758,759,762,763,766,767,770,771,433,774,777],{},"The chain order matters: the grammar sampler restricts the candidate\ntoken set, and ",[226,760,761],{},"greedy"," (or any downstream sampler) picks one. The\n",[226,764,765],{},"unsafe"," is required because the C strings the grammar sampler wraps\nmust outlive the sampler, which is the case here because\n",[226,768,769],{},"grammar_text"," is a local ",[226,772,773],{},"String",[226,775,776],{},"llama"," outlives the call.",[264,779,781],{"id":780},"tools-versus-structured-output","Tools versus structured output",[223,783,784],{},"Use structured output when the response itself must match a schema. Use\na tool-call pattern when the model should choose or populate an action\nthat your Rust code will execute.",[223,786,787,790],{},[226,788,789],{},"llama_crab::chat::tool_call"," provides:",[368,792,793,799,808,817],{},[371,794,795,798],{},[226,796,797],{},"ToolDefinition"," — a JSON-Schema-shaped tool description.",[371,800,801,804,805,241],{},[226,802,803],{},"ToolCall"," — a parsed invocation ",[226,806,807],{},"{ id, name, arguments }",[371,809,810,421,813,816],{},[226,811,812],{},"ToolParser",[226,814,815],{},"extract_tool_calls"," — non-streaming parser for a\ncomplete response.",[371,818,819,822,823,380,826,829,830,433,833,836],{},[226,820,821],{},"ToolCallStream"," — OpenAI-style streaming deltas with ",[226,824,825],{},"id",[226,827,828],{},"name",",\n",[226,831,832],{},"arguments",[226,834,835],{},"completed"," fields.",[223,838,839,840,843,844,847,848,850,851,853,854,857,858,861],{},"The ",[226,841,842],{},"tools"," example in ",[226,845,846],{},"llama-crab-examples"," demonstrates the practical\npattern: describe the tool in the system prompt, ask the model for a\nJSON call, parse the call with ",[226,849,815],{}," or ",[226,852,821],{},",\nexecute the function in Rust, then append a ",[226,855,856],{},"Role::Tool"," result message\nvia ",[226,859,860],{},"ChatMessage::tool_result(id, content)"," and continue the loop.",[264,863,865,866],{"id":864},"streaming-deltas-with-llguidance","Streaming deltas with ",[226,867,868],{},"llguidance",[223,870,871,873,874,876,877,879,880,883,884,887,888,890,891,893],{},[226,872,228],{}," also exposes the ",[226,875,868],{}," feature, which adds the\n",[226,878,868],{}," sampler as an alternative GBNF\u002FJSON-Schema backend. Enable\nit with ",[226,881,882],{},"features = [\"llguidance\"]","; the runtime API is the same —\nbuild a sampler with ",[226,885,886],{},"LlamaSampler::grammar"," (or the ",[226,889,868],{},"\nequivalent) and feed it into ",[226,892,240],{},". The\nbackend has different performance characteristics and is mostly useful\nwhen you need its constrained-decoding capabilities on top of an\nexisting prompt grammar.",[264,895,897],{"id":896},"operational-notes","Operational notes",[368,899,900,915,926],{},[371,901,839,902,905,906,908,909,911,912,914],{},[226,903,904],{},"grammar"," sampler requires the ",[226,907,251],{}," feature on the\n",[226,910,255],{}," build. If you disable default features, make sure\n",[226,913,251],{}," is enabled (or that the GBNF string is simple enough for the\ngrammar-free samplers).",[371,916,917,918,921,922,925],{},"Stop strings, logit biases and the ",[226,919,920],{},"min_tokens"," guard from\n",[226,923,924],{},"CompletionOptions"," work alongside the grammar sampler — but a stop\nstring that fires before a value is complete will truncate the\noutput, so prefer schema constraints when correctness matters.",[371,927,928,929,932,933,936],{},"After generation, parse and validate the response with ",[226,930,931],{},"serde_json","\n(and ",[226,934,935],{},"jsonschema"," for stricter validation) before treating it as\nwell-formed.",[938,939,940],"style",{},"html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki s